\section{Introduction}
Traditional spacecraft station-keeping strategies rely on open-loop propellant consumption to counteract solar radiation pressure and gravitational instabilities in multi-body regimes. In this work, we introduce a conservative control architecture driven by telemetry-derived cryptographic keys to achieve micro-Newton-scale trajectory stabilization. By enforcing $\nabla \times \mathbf{F}_{\text{ctrl}} = \mathbf{0}$, total mechanical energy remains conserved across closed spatial loops ($\oint \mathbf{F}_{\text{ctrl}} \cdot d\mathbf{r} = 0$).

% ---------------------------------------------------------
% II. Governing Equations
