\section{Restricted Three-Body Framework}
In the rotating Sun-Earth reference frame, the baseline system is governed by the restricted three-body effective potential:
\begin{equation}
\Omega(x,y,z) = \frac{1}{2}(x^2 + y^2) + \frac{1-\mu}{r_1} + \frac{\mu}{r_2}
\end{equation}
The total force vector incorporates the engineered scalar potential $\Phi(r, \theta, \phi; D(t))$ driven by observational data stream $D(t)$:
\begin{equation}
\mathbf{F}_{\text{total}} = \mathbf{F}_{\text{grav+rot}} - \nabla \Phi(r, \theta, \phi; D(t)) + \mathbf{F}_{\text{rad}}
\end{equation}

