\section{Stability Analysis \& Stochastic Dropout Resilience}
The total system Hessian $H_{\text{tot}} = H_{\Omega} + H_{\Phi}$ is integrated into the linearized $6 \times 6$ stability matrix $\mathbf{A}(t)$, mapping instantaneous eigenspectrum shifts. Telemetry dropouts and key state degradation are modeled via a continuous-time Markov process with transition rates $\lambda$ (dropout) and $\mu$ (recovery), proving bounded excursion probabilities under stochastic perturbations.

